00:35:28.809 --> 00:35:30.449
Well, that's the other thing to your point, Josh.
嗯，顺着你的话说，乔什，这也是另一回事。

00:35:30.449 --> 00:35:42.769
Like you think you're pushing your life in one way and you think at some point you were like, oh, that didn't work.
就像你以为自己在某个方向上推动着生活，在某个时刻你会觉得，“哦，那没成功。”

00:35:42.769 --> 00:35:49.969
But you were actually influencing the direction of your life, just in your career, just in ways that you weren't aware of.
但实际上你一直在影响着生活和职业的方向，只是以你当时没有意识到 Są 的方式。

00:35:49.969 --> 00:35:50.809
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:35:50.809 --> 00:35:58.530
Like, there's, there is a sort of a path there, but it's not one that you're creating or that you're kind of in charge.
就像，那里确实有一条路，但它不是由你创造的，也不是你在掌控的。

00:35:58.530 --> 00:36:14.289
Yeah, it's almost like partnering with mysterious forces where some of it, you have agency around, you have control of what you say as to and over what you say no to, you have control over your conduct on set, like you said, like trying not to be a kind, good person to work with.
是的，这几乎就像是与某种神秘力量合作，其中一部分你有自主权，你可以控制自己说什么以及对什么说不，你可以控制自己在片场上的行为，就像你说的，努力做一个善良、好合作的人。

00:36:14.289 --> 00:36:17.329
like you don't wanna be put in the life's too short category.
就像你不想被归入“人生苦短”那一类（让人觉得不值得合作）里。

00:36:17.329 --> 00:36:34.369
But a lot of it is just, you know, strange, like you're depending on, in some ways, like the reason Craig wanted to cast all of you guys is because I think when you make someone laugh, there's this gratitude where you're like, thank you, life is hard, you made me laugh.
但很大程度上只是，你知道，很奇妙，在某种程度上，克雷格想选定你们所有人的原因，是因为我认为当一个人逗笑别人时，会有一种感激之情，你会觉得：谢谢你，生活很艰难，你逗笑了我。

00:36:34.369 --> 00:36:35.210
You remember it.
你会记住它。

00:36:35.210 --> 00:36:36.050
You remember the feeling.
你会记住那种感觉。

00:36:36.050 --> 00:36:37.889
I remember that feeling.
我记得那种感觉。

00:36:37.889 --> 00:36:38.730
Yeah.
是啊。

00:36:38.730 --> 00:36:45.929
The people that have made me laugh really hard, whether it's in life or in performance, like I have an like unending gratitude for them.
那些曾让我开怀大笑的人，无论是在生活中还是在表演中，我都对他们充满无尽的感激。

00:36:45.929 --> 00:36:46.769
Yeah.
是的。

00:36:46.769 --> 00:36:48.650
I completely feel the same way.
我完全有同感。

00:36:48.650 --> 00:37:04.969
And to piggyback on that, the comedic performance that I love, that I performers that I love the most, for some reason I'm convinced that they're selfless about it.
顺着这个话题说，我最喜欢的喜剧表演者，出于某种原因，我坚信他们在表演时是无私的。

00:37:04.969 --> 00:37:08.170
Like they're not trying to be clever.
就像他们不是在刻意耍小聪明。

00:37:08.170 --> 00:37:10.489
They're not trying to convince you of anything.
他们不想向你证明什么。

00:37:10.489 --> 00:37:20.190
they're not trying to tell you that they're smart or anything, they're just trying to make that sound come out of your body.
他们不是想向你展示他们有多聪明，他们只是想让你发出笑声。

00:37:20.190 --> 00:37:22.150
And they'll do whatever takes it.
而且他们会不惜一切代价做到这一点。

00:37:22.150 --> 00:37:24.150
It's like music, it's pretty pure.
这就像音乐一样，非常纯粹。

00:37:24.150 --> 00:37:30.630
It's, yeah, when I sense that in a performer, I go, oh, I love you, you know, it's...
就是，是的，当我从一个表演者身上感受到这一点时，我就会想，哦，我太喜欢你了，你知道，这……

00:37:30.630 --> 00:37:31.469
I love that.
我太喜欢这样了。

00:37:31.469 --> 00:37:32.949
Well, we love you, John Cho.
好吧，我们也很喜欢你，约翰·赵。

00:37:32.949 --> 00:37:34.389
We can't take it for your whole night.
我们不能占用你一整晚的时间。

00:37:34.389 --> 00:37:35.469
You were so nice to do this.
你能来真是太好了。

00:37:35.469 --> 00:37:38.269
This was like, we were talking about the episode separately from this.
这就像是，我们在录制之前就单独讨论过这一集。

00:37:38.269 --> 00:37:40.070
We're like, we gotta have John on here.
我们当时就在想，我们一定要请约翰上节目。

00:37:40.070 --> 00:37:43.150
So I'm so, oh my God, I'm so glad that we did.
所以天哪，我太高兴我们真的这么做了。

00:37:43.150 --> 00:37:44.150
Thank you for making the time.
谢谢你抽出时间。

00:37:44.150 --> 00:37:45.750
I know we had to go back and forth a little bit.
我知道我们之前为此协调了好几次。

00:37:45.750 --> 00:37:46.590
Yeah, man.
对的，兄弟。

00:37:46.590 --> 00:37:47.429
Thanks so much.
非常感谢。

00:37:47.429 --> 00:37:48.269
Great to see you, man.
很高兴见到你，兄弟。

00:37:48.269 --> 00:37:49.110
I hope to see you soon.
希望不久能再见到你。

00:37:49.110 --> 00:37:49.949
Thanks, guys.
谢谢你们，伙计们。

00:37:49.949 --> 00:37:50.949
This is fun.
这很有趣。

00:37:50.949 --> 00:37:53.340
I am guilty.
我有罪。

00:37:53.340 --> 00:37:55.260
Please equip me.
请赐予我救赎吧。

00:37:55.260 --> 00:37:57.539
All sins are forgiven.
所有的罪孽都被原谅了。

00:37:57.539 --> 00:38:00.019
In New York City.
在纽约市。

